{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.118.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2011-3389-libgnutls30t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2011-3389 low vulnerability for libgnutls30t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The SSL protocol, as used in certain configurations in Microsoft Windows and Microsoft Internet Explorer, Mozilla Firefox, Google Chrome, Opera, and other products, encrypts data by using CBC mode with chained initialization vectors, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to obtain plaintext HTTP headers via a blockwise chosen-boundary attack (BCBA) on an HTTPS session, in conjunction with JavaScript code that uses (1) the HTML5 WebSocket API, (2) the Java URLConnection API, or (3) the Silverlight WebClient API, aka a \"BEAST\" attack."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2011-3389",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2011-3389\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libgnutls30t64\nVersion: 3.8.9-3+deb13u4\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2011-3389](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2011-3389)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2011-3389**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libgnutls30t64  | 3.8.9-3+deb13u4  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2011-3389](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2011-3389)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libgnutls30t64@3.8.9-3%2Bdeb13u4?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=gnutls28"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9079-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-9079 critical vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libcurl had a flaw that when instructed to clear proxy authentication credentials which made it not do so, leaving the old credentials around to get used for subsequent transfers that should not know nor use them."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9079",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-9079\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.14.1-2+deb13u5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-9079](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9079)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-9079**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | curl  | 8.14.1-2+deb13u5  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-9079](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-9079)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.14.1-2%2Bdeb13u5?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
