            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-13221-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-13221 critical vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions before 5.40.5-RC1, from 5.41.0 before 5.42.3-RC1, from 5.43.0 before 5.43.10 produce silently incorrect regular expression matches when an alternation of more than 65535 fixed string branches is compiled into a trie in Perl_study_chunk.  When such branches are combined into a trie, the delta between the first branch and the shared tail is stored in a 16-bit field. A branch count above 65535 overflows the field, and the trie's match decision table is truncated with no warning or error.  A pattern of this shape produces false positive matches (matching strings it should not) and false negative matches (failing to match strings it should). When such a pattern gates an access or filtering decision, the result is wrong."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-13221",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-13221\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.40.1-6+deb13u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-13221](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-13221)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-13221**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | perl-base  | 5.40.1-6+deb13u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-13221](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-13221)  |\n"
