              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-13608 high vulnerability for libcurl4t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in the libcurl SASL negotiation for LDAP authentication allows an incomplete handshake sequence to be misinterpreted as a successful cryptographic verification. An attacker executing a Man-in-the-Middle (MITM) attack can inject a premature or shortcut response that bypasses complete peer validation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-13608",
              "help": {
