            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42497-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42497 high vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Archive::Tar versions before 3.08 for Perl extract hardlinks to attacker controlled paths outside the extraction directory.  _make_special_file() passes the tar header's linkname to link() without validating it against absolute paths or .. segments, creating a hardlink that shares the victim file's inode.  A subsequent write through the extracted name modifies the victim file, and the post-extraction chmod, chown, and utime block in _extract_file() (guarded only against symlinks via -l) applies the tar header's mode, owner, and timestamps to the shared inode during extraction alone."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42497",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42497\nSeverity: high\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.40.1-6+deb13u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-42497](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42497)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42497**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | perl-base  | 5.40.1-6+deb13u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-42497](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42497)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.40.1-6%2Bdeb13u1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8458-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8458 medium vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libcurl might in some circumstances reuse the wrong connection when asked to do Negotiate-authenticated ones, even when they are set to use different 'services'.  libcurl features a pool of recent connections so that subsequent requests can reuse an existing connection to avoid overhead.  When reusing a connection a range of criteria must be met. Due to a logical error in the code, a request that was issued by an application could wrongfully reuse an existing connection to the same server that was authenticated using different services."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8458",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8458\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.14.1-2+deb13u5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-8458](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8458)",
