            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41992-gzip",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-41992 high vulnerability for gzip package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU gzip contains a global buffer overflow vulnerability in the LZH decompression logic caused by improper reuse of shared global state between different decompression formats within a single execution. GNU gzip maintains a global array that is shared across the LZ77, LZW, and LZH decompression routines and is not reinitialized between files processed in the same invocation. By decompressing a specially crafted LZW file followed by a specially crafted LZH file in a single gzip -d command, an attacker can poison the shared global state and subsequently trigger an out‑of‑bounds read in the LZH decoder. The LZH decompression logic follows stale values left in the shared array, causing reads past the end of the allocated global buffer.  This issue has been fixed in commits 63dbf6b3b9e6e781df1a6a64e609b10e23969681 and e7378c2d421be6a286922374425680bbe9ad8b7d."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-41992",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41992\nSeverity: high\nPackage: gzip\nVersion: 1.13-1+deb13u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-41992](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-41992)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41992**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | gzip  | 1.13-1+deb13u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-41992](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-41992)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/gzip@1.13-1%2Bdeb13u1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-66034-libssh2-1t64",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-66034 high vulnerability for libssh2-1t64 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libssh2 through 1.11.1, fixed in commit a13bb6c, contains a missing bounds check vulnerability that allows a malicious SSH server to trigger an arbitrary-length heap out-of-bounds read and a free of an uninitialized pointer via the publickey subsystem. In libssh2_publickey_list_fetch(), the version 1 response parser reads a server-controlled comment_len value and advances the parse pointer without verifying sufficient bytes remain in the buffer, causing the out-of-bounds read to leak heap pointers from adjacent allocations defeating ASLR, followed by heap allocator state corruption when the error cleanup path frees an uninitialized pointer from a non-zeroed realloc() region."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66034",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-66034\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libssh2-1t64\nVersion: 1.11.1-1+deb13u2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-66034](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66034)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-66034**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libssh2-1t64  | 1.11.1-1+deb13u2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-66034](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66034)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libssh2-1t64@1.11.1-1%2Bdeb13u2?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=libssh2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80230-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-80230 high vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When `CURLOPT_PINNEDPUBLICKEY` is configured alongside options that disable standard peer verification (`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER = 0` and `CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST = 0`), libcurl fails to enforce public key pinning on connections established without a presented server certificate. Bypassing the pinning check under these disabled-verification conditions allows unauthenticated connections to succeed when they should be rejected."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-80230",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80230\nSeverity: high\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.14.1-2+deb13u5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-80230](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-80230)",
