            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-57432-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-57432 high vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions before 5.40.5-RC1, from 5.41.0 before 5.42.3-RC1, from 5.43.0 before 5.43.11 have an integer overflow in S_measure_struct leading to an out-of-bounds heap read in pack and unpack.  S_measure_struct adds each item's size times its repeat count to a running total with no overflow check, so a large repeat count in a pack or unpack template wraps the signed SSize_t total negative. The @, X, and x position codes then guard their moves with a signed length comparison that passes when the length is negative, advancing the buffer pointer out of bounds.  A template derived from untrusted input can read heap memory past the buffer and return it to the caller."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-57432",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-57432\nSeverity: high\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.40.1-6+deb13u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-57432](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-57432)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-57432**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | perl-base  | 5.40.1-6+deb13u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-57432](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-57432)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
