            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-15534-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-15534 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions through 5.45.1 have out-of-bounds heap reads and writes during regular expression matching via an undersized superlinear cache in S_regmatch.  The regex engine's superlinear cache holds one bit per subject position for each participating WHILEM node, so the bit count is the subject length plus one times the number of nodes. Nothing checks that product for positive overflow of the signed 32-bit count: a 286331153 byte subject matched against a pattern with 15 participating nodes stores the count as 14, leaving a two byte cache. The cache is then indexed from the real match position and node number, so reads go past the end of the allocation, and on failure CACHEsayNO sets a bit past it.  A caller that matches an attacker controlled subject of this size against a pattern of this shape can crash the process or corrupt heap memory."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15534",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-15534\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.40.1-6+deb13u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-15534](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15534)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-15534**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.40.1-6+deb13u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-15534](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15534)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.40.1-6%2Bdeb13u1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78408-bsdutils",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-78408 high vulnerability for bsdutils package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The nsenter --join-cgroup option opens the target cgroup.procs file as root and leaves that file descriptor open across later namespace and credential changes and across execve(). Because the kernel checks later cgroup migrations using the credentials from the original open, a program run in an attacker-controlled target can inherit root's ability to move host processes between cgroups. After a privileged operator uses --join-cgroup against that target, an unprivileged user can migrate and terminate unrelated root processes."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-78408",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-78408\nSeverity: high\nPackage: bsdutils\nVersion: 1:2.41.5-0+deb13u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-78408](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-78408)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-78408**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | bsdutils  | 1:2.41.5-0+deb13u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:13  | [CVE-2026-78408](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-78408)  |\n"
              },
