              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libp11-kit0@0.25.5-3?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian-13.7\u0026upstream=p11-kit"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-54371-libattr1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-54371 medium vulnerability for libattr1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "attr before version 2.6.0 contains a symlink traversal vulnerability in the getfattr and setfattr utilities that allows local attackers to escalate privileges by replacing a pathname component with a symbolic link during directory hierarchy traversal. Attackers who control a pathname component can redirect getfattr and setfattr operations to arbitrary files by substituting a symlink, leading to local privilege escalation when getfattr or setfattr is invoked by a privileged process over an attacker-controlled path."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-54371",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-54371\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libattr1\nVersion: 1:2.5.2-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:13\nLink: [CVE-2026-54371](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-54371)",
